# MegaLens — FAIL streak vs ship intake

## Track consecutive FAILs

In **AUDIT_DEBT.md** section `## Consecutive FAILs (MegaLens gate)`:

```
Feature area: [e.g. map pins / layout / time]
Streak: N
Last versions: v1.1.4 FAIL, v1.1.5 FAIL, v1.1.6 FAIL
Reset on: PASS on that feature | new feature area | MegaLens APPROVED run
```

Update streak every user test FAIL on the **same feature area** (map pins, layout, etc.).

## When streak hits 3 → MegaLens BEFORE next build

1. Do **not** send thin handoff to Builder yet
2. Tell user (required tone):

   > **LET'S MEGALENSE THIS SHIT UP.** Level 3 (~$0.22). Three FAILs on [area]. Say: `run standard megalens, I accept ~$0.22`

3. Wait for exact phrase — then L3 per `megalens-operator-manual.mdc`
4. MegaLens findings → **FULL BUILDER HANDOFF** (`builder-handoff-full-spec.mdc`)
5. Reset streak after PASS or after user declines MegaLens and accepts static-only handoff (note in AUDIT_DEBT)

## Ship intake = NO MegaLens by default

User pastes **BUILDER SHIP HANDOFF** → `auditor-builder-ship-intake.mdc` (logs + grep + Original mod, $0).

MegaLens on intake only if streak ≥ 3 **and** user already approved spend, or user asks unprompted.

## Streak does NOT count

- Version not installed (log L3 ≠ shipped version) — **install gate**, not feature FAIL
- User error (wrong zip, didn't overwrite Fluffy)
- PASS on unrelated feature while map still broken — map streak continues
